---
globs: src/aquawatch/detectors.py, src/aquawatch/model.py, src/aquawatch/baseline.py, src/aquawatch/pipeline.py, src/aquawatch/metrics.py, src/aquawatch/report.py, src/aquawatch/settings.py, configs/default.toml
alwaysApply: false
---

When you change detection or evaluation code:

- All training must be label-free.
  - `fit_detector` and every baseline may read only flow, pressure, time and zone.
  - Labels are for `src/aquawatch/metrics.py` scoring only.
- Thresholds in `configs/default.toml` are fixed in advance. Do not change them to improve test results. Tuning needs a separate validation window, documented in the code and docs.
- Every new detector is a class in `src/aquawatch/detectors.py` with `fit` (label-free), `score` and `alarms`, added to `REGISTRY`. Then:
  - the pipeline, metrics, report and app pick it up automatically
  - `tests/test_detectors.py` checks it automatically (no labels used, alarms follow score and threshold)
  - add a unit test of its logic in `tests/test_baselines.py`
- Refactors must keep `tests/test_golden_results.py` passing. Update the snapshot only for intended result changes, and explain why.
- Report results per event: events caught with a 95% CI, real/all alarms, false alarms per zone-week, and hours to detect.
- After a change, run `aquawatch evaluate --dataset simulated` and update `data/simulated/DATASHEET.md` if the numbers moved.
